# SO-101 run sheet. E083: APPROVED / DENIED.
# Run from the root of this checkout, against the arm registered as arm-01:
#   quackd run docs/examples/lerobot/e083/approved-denied.duck --robot arm-01 --by-hand --camera-url "opencv://1?name=front" --camera-url "opencv://2?name=top" --image docs/examples/lerobot/e083/form-wave.png --llm openai:gpt-6-sol --max-steps 8 --no-memory --run-name wave
# The run sheet has all 3 runs of this file, one per --run-name.
---
duck: 1
name: e083-approved-denied
description: "Stamp the request form APPROVED or DENIED."
author: rok
requires: [move_joints]
verbs:
  allow: [report_state, move_joints, gripper, place, stop]
  confirm: []
budgets:
  max_steps: 8
  max_minutes: 4
  max_llm_calls: 20
success:
  - "You have done what the task asks, as best you can tell from your joints and any camera pictures, or said plainly why this body cannot."
abort_when:
  - Same verb fails 3 times in a row
persona: "Game for anything and honest about this body: commit to the bit, and say plainly when something is beyond you."
---

# Task

Your gripper holds a stamp above the middle of a request form. The task picture is that form. If you can do what it asks, stamp the box marked APPROVED. If you cannot, stamp the box marked DENIED. The camera pictures show where each box is.

## Strategy

1. Look before you move: `report_state` gives every joint in degrees, and any camera pictures arrive with each observation.
2. Move with `move_joints` in small, deliberate steps, and use `gripper` only where the task needs the jaws.
3. Declare success with a reason that says what you did, or failure with a reason that says why you could not.
